  "summary": "Reverse shell on require to hardcoded remote endpoint",
  "details": "The gem's library entrypoint, executed unconditionally on `require 'zzhelloworld_socktest'`, opens a TCPSocket to the hardcoded host 66.78.40.218 on port 32768, reopens STDIN, STDOUT, and STDERR onto that socket, and execs `/bin/sh -i`. The result is an interactive shell on the installer's machine bound to the remote endpoint. The behavior fires on load with no authentication, no gating, and no disclosure in the gem's documentation.",
